; ted-outmem-in-blitz2-call (#369): blitz2 allocates through TED's
; extalloc; when an allocation fails during a compile, outmem shows the
; alert and jumps back into TED's main loop, over blitz2's frames: the
; compile is abandoned without blitz2's cleanup (its open includes stay
; open).  blitz2 under inject (alerts answered), a source that includes
; inc.bb2 (tokenised) with a macro of a 205-byte text, whose allocation
; fails once (any flags: the port clears the block, #970); CREATE
; EXECUTABLE twice, QUIT.
; Correct: the alert "Not enough memory for operation!" (TED's notice),
; blitz2 ends the first compile through its own cleanup (the include is
; closed), the second compile creates the executable and blitz2 ends
; normally.
; @fixed #369 Cc
; @file inc.bb2 "\x80\x0d m\x00a$=\"xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\"\x00\x80\x02 \x80\x0d\x00"
; @file bo.bas "Include \"TEDRUN:work/inc.bb2\"\n!m\nNPrint a$\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @command TEDAB:tools/inject alerts allocfail=205-205/1 inuse=TEDRUN:work/inc.bb2 blitz2:blitz2 @FILE@
; @expect stdout "inject: allocfail: 1 allocations failed"
; @expect stdout "inject: alert: Not enough memory for operation!"
; @expect stdout "inject: not in use: TEDRUN:work/inc.bb2"
; @expect stdout "inject: rc=0"
; @expect exists bo
timeout 20
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
menu 4 2
wait freq "Name of Executable to create"
timeout 30
freq ok "bo" "TEDRUN:work"  ; @ignore compilewindow
timeout 10
wait screen
menu 4 2
wait freq "Name of Executable to create"
timeout 30
freq ok "bo" "TEDRUN:work"  ; @ignore compilewindow
timeout 10
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
